  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n- `posting::default_machine_checked()` reads the default machine file (`assets/machines/3axis-vmc.mch`) as a `Result`. `parse_default_machine` refuses a file in these cases:\r\n  - the file does not read;\r\n  - the file is not JSON;\r\n  - the file is not a JSON object;\r\n  - the object has no `name` or no `kinematics.static` object. These are the keys that the post reads for the header and the coolant words. The shipped `3axis-vmc.mch` has both.\r\n- The code is in the new module `crates/app/src/posting_default_machine.rs` (59 lines), not in `posting.rs`. `posting.rs` goes from 1547 to 1535 lines. #2322 tracks the full split.\r\n- A refusal is not kept until restart. Only a machine that passed the check is kept (`posting::KeptMachine`). `default_mch_text` reads at each call and keeps nothing. A failed read or a refused file is read again at the next post, so a repaired file posts without a restart.\r\n- `posting_mounts::posted_machine_for` is the one door from a mount to the engine's machine value. A mounted machine is mirrored as before. No mounted machine reads `default_machine_checked()` and refuses with `post blocked - ...`.\r\n- The three post paths use it: the single-file post (`post_script_body_with`), the per-mount post (`post_each`) and the per-operation post.\r\n- `default_machine()` keeps its `Value` form for the sim traverse clock (it writes no G-code).\r\n- `engine::run` with `Value::Null` stays a legal input (the `post` binary, the script check in `commands/post.rs`, the tests).\r\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2319-default-machine-refusal.md`.\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\nBefore the fix, with no default machine file or a malformed file, the CLI exits 0 and writes a complete program. Compared with the good file, the header reads `O0001 (CAMCRAFT)` in place of `O0001 (VMC 3-AXIS)`, and all `M8` / `M9` lines are gone. The issue comment has the details.\r\n\r\nAfter the fix, the CLI exits 1 and writes no file. The messages are:\r\n- `post blocked - the default machine file 3axis-vmc.mch cannot be read (<reason>) - mount a machine on the setup, or reinstall the file`\r\n- `post blocked - the default machine file 3axis-vmc.mch is malformed (<parse error> | not a machine object | it has no machine name | it has no kinematics.static section) - mount a machine on the setup, or reinstall the file`\r\n\r\nThe per-mount post puts the mount label in front (for example `Setup2: post blocked - ...`). The per-operation post puts the operation name in front (`Face2: post blocked - ...`).\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n`crates/app/tests/default_machine_missing.rs` (9 tests). The CLI tests spawn the real CLI beside a hand-made `assets/` folder:\r\n- `a_missing_default_machine_file_refuses_the_post`\r\n- `a_missing_default_machine_file_refuses_the_post_per_mount`: Setup1 mounted, Setup2 not mounted. Exit 1, names `Setup2` and the file, the output folder stays empty.\r\n- `a_missing_default_machine_file_refuses_the_post_per_operation`: the same document, one file per operation. Exit 1, names `Face2` and the file, the output folder stays empty.\r\n- `a_malformed_default_machine_file_refuses_the_post`\r\n- `an_empty_object_as_default_machine_file_refuses_the_post` (`{}`)\r\n- `a_good_default_machine_file_still_posts` (control, with `M8`)\r\n- `the_default_machine_file_must_be_a_machine_object` (unit: `[]`, `\"x\"`, `null`, `{}`, a blank name, no `kinematics.static`, a `static` array, an unreadable file)\r\n- `a_repaired_default_machine_file_is_read_again_and_a_good_one_is_kept` (unit: missing, then `{}`, then the good file give Err, Err, Ok; a later `{}` gives the kept machine)\r\n- `the_shipped_default_machine_file_is_accepted` (unit)\r\n\r\nMutations, each reverted after the run:\r\n\r\n| Mutation | Result |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `post_each` reads `machine_value_for` (null machine) again | `..._per_mount` fails |\r\n| The per-operation post reads `machine_value_for` again | `..._per_operation` fails |\r\n| The file text is kept as soon as it reads (the old caching) | `a_repaired_..._is_kept` fails |\r\n| `parse_default_machine` accepts any object | `an_empty_object_...` and `the_default_machine_file_must_be_a_machine_object` fail |\r\n\r\nOther targeted suites, all green: `golden_cl` (33), `post_not_judged` (4), `shipped_from_disk` (3), `solid_law_goldens` (7), `posting` (17), `per_op_files` (9), `per_op_script_options` (2), `setup_mounts_post` (8). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\r\n\r\n## Follow-up issues\r\n\r\n- #2321: the post does not check the default machine's limits for a document with no mounted machine (older gap, `P3`).\r\n- #2322: split `crates/app/src/posting.rs` (`P7`).\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The GUI post dialog and the MCP post tools. They call the same app post functions, but no test drives them here.\r\n- The re-read is tested through `KeptMachine` with a given reader, not through a running CLI process.\r\n- A default file with a name and a `kinematics.static` section but no limits still posts with the engine defaults (#2321).\r\n- No release build, no wasm build.\r\n\r\nChangelog: A missing or malformed default machine file now refuses the post with a message that names the file. Before, the post wrote a program with no coolant words and no machine name.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nFixes #2319\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
